From e927143a92ef08b4cdeb0846d75eb9fb44966235 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suvojeet-sengupta <suvojitsengupta21@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:22:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] camera: Keep privileged YUV and BLOB sizes as asked

Since the bypass was limited to sizes with no listed match, a
privileged app's YUV or BLOB stream is rounded to the nearest listed
size again. Xiaomi's camera asks for 12000x9000 YUV in its 108 MP mode,
a size the HAL lists only in its own vendor tags, so the stream became
a second 4000x3000 one. The HAL had no place for it, returned
max_buffers 0, and the session failed.

Bypass rounding for privileged YUV and BLOB streams again, as QTI does,
and keep it for every other format with no listed size.
---
 .../libcameraservice/utils/SessionConfigurationUtils.cpp       | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/camera/libcameraservice/utils/SessionConfigurationUtils.cpp b/services/camera/libcameraservice/utils/SessionConfigurationUtils.cpp
index 880cad1b2c..8caa432cd3 100644
--- a/services/camera/libcameraservice/utils/SessionConfigurationUtils.cpp
+++ b/services/camera/libcameraservice/utils/SessionConfigurationUtils.cpp
@@ -217,7 +217,8 @@ bool roundBufferDimensionNearest(int32_t width, int32_t height,
         }
     }
 
-    if (isPriviledgedClient == true && bestWidth == -1) {
+    if (isPriviledgedClient == true && (bestWidth == -1 ||
+            format == HAL_PIXEL_FORMAT_YCbCr_420_888 || format == HAL_PIXEL_FORMAT_BLOB)) {
         ALOGI("Bypass roundBufferDimensionNearest for privilegedClient "
                 "width %d height %d for format %d", width, height, format);
         bestWidth  = width;
-- 
2.43.0

